  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "NEW\n\t\t\t* Are for collections: items.Are(expected) asserts the same items in any order, and nothing more\n\t\t\t* Source.Projects for custom architecture rules: each project's dependencies and source files, with their lines and the types they declare\n\t\t\tIMPROVED\n\t\t\t* A failure counts the items of a collection, Empty() included\n\t\t\t* A failed Are, Like or EquivalentTo on a collection names the missing and the extra items\n\t\t\tFIXED\n\t\t\t* EquivalentTo and Like passed when the actual held more than expected; now they fail\n\t\t\t* Like and EquivalentTo never returned on an endless sequence compared with a collection\n\t\t\tOBSOLETE\n\t\t\t* Project.Dependencies: Source.Projects takes its place, and graph[\"X\"] is Source.Projects[\"X\"].Dependencies\n\t\t\tCHANGED\n\t\t\t* Requires xunit.v3 4.0.2 or later\n\t\t\tBREAKING - a passing test can turn red on upgrade\n\t\t\t* Like and EquivalentTo fail at setup when neither side is a collection, since either may never end",
